026 — No Signup, No Email, Instant Results\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"Free 2026 tax calculator with no signup, no email, no paywall. Calculate take-home pay, tax refund, self-employment tax, and more. CPA-reviewed accuracy.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-1\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",\"free\",{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-border/30 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[9px] text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"free\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"tax\",{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-border/30 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[9px] text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"tax\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"calculator\",{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-border/30 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[9px] text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"calculator\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"take-home-pay-calculator-guide-2026\",{\"href\":\"/blog/take-home-pay-calculator-guide-2026\",\"className\":\"group rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-card p-5 hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:shadow-md transition-all\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2 mb-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-medium bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/20 dark:text-emerald-400 border-emerald-300 dark:border-emerald-500/30\",\"children\":\"Tax Guide\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[10px] text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"June 21, 2026\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-emerald-600 dark:group-hover:text-emerald-400 transition-colors line-clamp-2 mb-1.5\",\"children\":\"Take Home Pay Calculator 2026: How Much You Actually Keep\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"Complete take-home pay guide for 2026. Calculate your net pay after federal, FICA, and state taxes. Real examples for every state. Free calculator, no signup.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-1\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",\"take\",{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-border/30 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[9px] text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"take\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"home\",{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-border/30 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[9px] text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"home\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"pay\",{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-border/30 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[9px] text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"pay\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"hourly-wage-after-tax-questions-2026\",{\"href\":\"/blog/hourly-wage-after-tax-questions-2026\",\"className\":\"group rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-card p-5 hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:shadow-md transition-all\",\"children\":[\"$L11\",\"$L12\",\"$L13\",\"$L14\"]}]]}]]}]\nc:[\"$\",\"script\",\"script-0\",{\"src\":\"/_next/static/chunks/2d86c01f2aacd453.js\",\"async\":true}]\nd:[\"$\",\"$L15\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$16\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@17\"}]}]\n18:Tca5,<p>Wondering \"how much tax will I owe in 2026?\" You're not alone. It's one of the most common tax questions Americans ask every year — and for good reason. The US tax code is notoriously complex, with seven federal brackets, multiple filing statuses, FICA payroll taxes, state income taxes (in 41 states plus DC), and dozens of deductions and credits that can dramatically change your final bill.</p><p>This guide breaks down exactly how to calculate your 2026 tax liability step by step. Whether you're a W-2 employee, self-employed freelancer, retiree, or somewhere in between, you'll find concrete numbers and worked examples that match your situation.</p><h2 id=\"quick-answer-how-much-tax-will-i-owe\">Quick Answer: How Much Tax Will I Owe?</h2><p>The short answer: it depends on your income, filing status, state, and deductions. But here are rough estimates for a single filer taking the standard deduction in 2026:</p><div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table><thead><tr><th>Gross Income</th><th>Federal Tax</th><th>FICA (7.65%)</th><th>Estimated State Tax</th><th>Total Tax</th><th>Effective Rate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>$30,000</td><td>$1,398</td><td>$2,295</td><td>$900</td><td>$4,593</td><td>15.3%</td></tr><tr><td>$50,000</td><td>$3,919</td><td>$3,825</td><td>$1,500</td><td>$9,244</td><td>18.5%</td></tr><tr><td>$75,000</td><td>$7,671</td><td>$5,738</td><td>$2,250</td><td>$15,659</td><td>20.9%</td></tr><tr><td>$100,000</td><td>$13,382</td><td>$7,650</td><td>$3,000</td><td>$24,032</td><td>24.0%</td></tr><tr><td>$150,000</td><td>$26,402</td><td>$11,475</td><td>$4,500</td><td>$42,377</td><td>28.3%</td></tr><tr><td>$200,000</td><td>$40,822</td><td>$12,921</td><td>$6,000</td><td>$59,743</td><td>29.9%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Use our free <a href=\"/paycheck-calculator\">2026 tax calculator</a> for personalized numbers.</p><h2 id=\"step-1-calculate-your-federal-income-tax\">Step 1: Calculate Your Federal Income Tax</h2><p>Federal income tax uses a progressive bracket system. The 2026 brackets for single filers: 10% ($0-$11,925), 12% ($11,926-$48,475), 22% ($48,476-$103,350), 24% ($103,351-$197,300), 32% ($197,301-$250,525), 35% ($250,526-$626,350), 37% (over $626,350).</p><h2 id=\"step-2-add-fica-payroll-taxes-7-65\">Step 2: Add FICA Payroll Taxes (7.65%)</h2><p>FICA funds Social Security (6.2% up to $184,500 wage base) and Medicare (1.45%, no cap). Total: 7.65% of gross wages.</p><h2 id=\"step-3-calculate-state-income-tax\">Step 3: Calculate State Income Tax</h2><p>Eight states have no income tax: Alaska, Florida, Nevada, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Washington, Wyoming. Other states range from 1% (North Dakota) to 13.3% (California).</p><h2 id=\"step-4-subtract-pre-tax-deductions\">Step 4: Subtract Pre-Tax Deductions</h2><p>401(k) up to $24,500, Traditional IRA up to $7,000, HSA up to $4,400 (self). These lower your taxable income.</p><h2 id=\"step-5-apply-tax-credits\">Step 5: Apply Tax Credits</h2><p>Child Tax Credit ($2,000/child), EITC (up to $7,430), American Opportunity Credit ($2,500/student), Saver's Credit ($1,000).</p><h2 id=\"step-6-calculate-your-total-tax-bill\">Step 6: Calculate Your Total Tax Bill</h2><p>Total Tax = Federal Income Tax + FICA + State Income Tax - Tax Credits</p>f:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto max-w-3xl lg:mx-0 lg:flex-1\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"prose-container\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$18\"}}]}]\n10:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto max-w-3xl mt-8\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors\",\"children\":\"← Back to Blog\"}]}]\n11:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2 mb-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-medium bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/20 dark:text-emerald-400 border-emerald-300 dark:border-emerald-500/30\",\"children\":\"Tax Guide\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[10px] text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"June 21, 2026\"}]]}]\n12:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-emerald-600 dark:group-hover:text-emerald-400 transition-colors line-clamp-2 mb-1.5\",\"children\":\"Hourly Wage After Tax Questions Answered (2026 Calculator)\"}]\n13:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"How much tax is taken out of a $300 paycheck? How much is $20/hour after taxes? $21/hour annually? $1200/week? Exact numbers for common wages with free calculator.\"}]\n14:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-1\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",\"hourly\",{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-border/30 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[9px] text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"hourly\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"wage\",{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-border/30 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[9px] text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"wage\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"after\",{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-border/30 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[9px] text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"after\"}]]}]\n17:null\n","/blog/$d$slug":"1:\"$Sreact.fragment\"\n2:I[39756,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/61cc43b3d7ad2990.js\"],\"default\"]\n3:I[37457,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/61cc43b3d7ad2990.js\"],\"default\"]\n0:{\"buildId\":\"DHHyHh_Ff3S5PG3AajNLG\",\"rsc\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{}]}]]}],\"loading\":null,\"isPartial\":false}\n","/blog":"1:\"$Sreact.fragment\"\n2:I[39756,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/61cc43b3d7ad2990.js\"],\"default\"]\n3:I[84040,[\"/_next/static/chunks/49e33bee669819de.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/868a9c4503c53c54.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/d791dd6e73034ab4.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/4b0a94d5243a034f.js\"],\"default\"]\n4:I[37457,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/61cc43b3d7ad2990.js\"],\"default\"]\n0:{\"buildId\":\"DHHyHh_Ff3S5PG3AajNLG\",\"rsc\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"error\":\"$3\",\"errorStyles\":[],\"errorScripts\":[[\"$\",\"script\",\"script-0\",{\"src\":\"/_next/static/chunks/4b0a94d5243a034f.js\",\"async\":true}]],\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{}]}]]}],\"loading\":null,\"